---
// A museum piece: the July 2025 three-vendor well-location comparison
// from the Databricks Asset Bundle experiment, served static. The
// dataset is frozen; the map replaces the original Streamlit app.
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Kingfisher Wells</title>
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://kingfisher.purr.io/" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Do well surface locations from S&P Global, Enverus and the OCC agree? Mostly. A three-vendor location-variance study of Kingfisher County, Oklahoma."
    />
      <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@400;600;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <nav class="topnav">
      <a class="logo" href="https://purr.io" aria-label="purr.io">
        <img src="/purrio_2026.png" alt="purr.io logo" />
      </a>
      <span class="brand">Kingfisher Wells</span>
      <a href="https://github.com/rbhughes/kingfisher_wells">GitHub</a>
      <span class="vintage">frozen snapshot &middot; July 2025</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="masthead">
      <h1>Do the lat/lons from different vendors agree with each other?
        <em>Mostly!</em></h1>
      <p class="tagline">
        The surface locations of every well in Kingfisher County,
        Oklahoma, as reported by
        <a href="https://www.spglobal.com/commodity-insights/en/products-solutions/upstream-midstream-oil-gas">S&amp;P Global</a>,
        <a href="https://www.enverus.com/products/enverus-core/">Enverus</a>,
        and the
        <a href="https://gisdata-occokc.opendata.arcgis.com/">Oklahoma
        Corporation Commission</a>, compared pairwise. Spoiler:
        <strong>about 3% of wells are misplaced by more than 500 meters
        relative to each other.</strong> That is roughly 250 wells in a
        single county. We don&rsquo;t know who is right, but we know
        somebody is wrong.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="controls">
      <div class="slider-wrap">
        <label for="threshold" id="threshold-label">
          disagreement &gt; 500 m</label>
        <input type="range" id="threshold" min="1" max="4" step="0.01"
          value="2.699" />
      </div>
      <input type="search" id="api-filter" autocomplete="off"
        placeholder="Filter by 10-digit API (35073…)" />
      <span class="counts" id="counts"></span>
      <div class="legend" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="swatch" style="--c: #2a78d6"></span><span>OCC</span>
        <span class="swatch" style="--c: #eb6834"></span><span>Enverus</span>
        <span class="swatch" style="--c: #1baf7a"></span><span>S&amp;P Global</span>
        <span class="line-swatch"></span><span>same well</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <main class="layout">
      <div id="map" class="map-box" role="application"
        aria-label="Well location disagreement map"></div>
      <aside class="panel">
        <h2>Worst offenders shown</h2>
        <p class="panel-note">
          Ranked by the largest pairwise disagreement. Click a row to
          locate the well; the gray lines connect one well&rsquo;s three
          reported positions.
        </p>
        <table class="offenders" id="offenders">
          <thead><tr>
            <th scope="col">Well</th>
            <th scope="col" class="num"
              title="Largest pairwise distance, meters">max&nbsp;m</th>
          </tr></thead>
          <tbody></tbody>
        </table>
      </aside>
    </main>

    <section class="chart-row">
      <div>
        <h2>How wrong, how often?</h2>
        <p class="chart-note">
          Distribution of each well&rsquo;s <em>largest</em> pairwise
          disagreement. Most triplets agree within tens of meters; the
          marker shows the current threshold.
        </p>
      </div>
      <svg id="hist" width="640" height="180" role="img"
        aria-label="Histogram of largest pairwise disagreement"></svg>
    </section>

    <article class="story">
      <h2>The medallion pipeline that built this</h2>
      <p>
        This dataset came out of a
        <a href="https://www.databricks.com/glossary/medallion-architecture">Medallion
        Architecture</a> exercise on Databricks, deployed as a
        <a href="https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/dev-tools/bundles">Databricks
        Asset Bundle</a> with CI/CD &mdash; the point was to learn and
        document that machinery on a real question, and the question
        turned out to have a real answer.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Bronze.</strong> Raw CSVs pulled from the Enverus and
          OCC web APIs (plus an S&amp;P export), filtered to
          <code>county = 'KINGFISHER'</code> with no other cleaning,
          each loaded into its own Delta table.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Silver.</strong> Identity columns and surface
          lat/lon standardized per source. S&amp;P reports NAD27, so
          its coordinates were transformed to WGS84 to match the other
          two. Points were deliberately <em>not</em> cleaned &mdash; the
          disagreements are the subject, not noise.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Gold.</strong> The three silver tables unioned and
          pivoted wide, one row per well, with pairwise distances via
          <code>ST_DISTANCESPHEROID</code>. Wells missing any vendor
          were dropped, leaving 8,339 &ldquo;triplets.&rdquo;
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The gold table was exported to parquet, and that file &mdash;
        committed to the repo &mdash; is what this page serves. A
        <a href="https://github.com/rbhughes/kingfisher_wells/blob/main/tests/test_snapshot_integrity.py">sanity
        check</a> recomputes every pairwise distance from the
        snapshot&rsquo;s own points with DuckDB&rsquo;s spheroid math:
        worst disagreement with the stored Databricks values, about
        <strong>5 microns</strong> across ~25,000 pairs.
      </p>

      <h2>What the disagreements look like</h2>
      <p>
        At low thresholds you see the expected: many S&amp;P points
        shifted a consistent few dozen meters north-east of their
        siblings, the signature of a NAD27&rarr;WGS84 datum history.
        Above a few hundred meters the excuses run out: wrong
        longitude quadrant signs, wells filed in the wrong county, and
        placements that disagree by kilometers. This is not a data
        cleaning exercise &mdash; it is an argument for never trusting a
        single vendor&rsquo;s coordinates without a second opinion.
      </p>

      <h2>The Databricks Asset Bundle experiment</h2>
      <p>
        The original app was Streamlit, deployed to Databricks as an
        Asset Bundle with GitHub Actions for tests and deploys. The
        <a href="https://github.com/rbhughes/kingfisher_wells#process">repo
        README</a> preserves the full step-by-step &mdash; bundle
        config, service principals, cluster grants, CI secrets &mdash;
        as it worked in August 2025. Highlights from the trenches:
      </p>
      <figure>
        <img src="/images/medallion_job.png"
          alt="Databricks job running bronze, silver and gold notebooks" />
        <figcaption>The medallion job: bronze &rarr; silver &rarr; gold
          notebooks in series.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Spatial SQL on Databricks was the hard part: Sedona wanted
          init scripts, Mosaic wanted old Spark, and the answer was the
          then-beta DBR 17.1 with native spatial &mdash; which in turn
          broke <code>databricks-connect</code> local development.
        </li>
        <li>
          SQL Warehouses didn&rsquo;t support spatial functions, so the
          app had to sit on an interactive cluster. $ouch$.
        </li>
        <li>
          Performance on the cluster was surprisingly poor for 30k
          rows of simple points; DuckDB against local parquet was
          instant. That observation is, in a sense, why this page is
          now a static site.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted">
        The Databricks workspace is gone; the pipeline, the app, and
        the walkthrough remain documented in the repo. This page is the
        museum: the July 2025 snapshot, served flat, with the map
        rebuilt in MapLibre.
      </p>
    </article>

    <footer>
      <p>
        Data: S&amp;P Global, Enverus, and Oklahoma Corporation
        Commission exports, July 2025, Kingfisher County, Oklahoma.
        Vendor coordinates shown as reported (WGS84-normalized);
        no cleaning applied. Basemap tiles by
        <a href="https://openfreemap.org">OpenFreeMap</a>.
        Code: <a href="https://github.com/rbhughes/kingfisher_wells">kingfisher_wells</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="colophon">A <a href="https://purr.io">purr.io</a> project &middot; &copy; 2026 &middot; built in the open</p>
    </footer>

    <script src="../scripts/app.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  :root {
    --page: #f3f4f6;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --ink: #262e42;
    --ink-2: #5b6577;
    --muted: #9aa0ab;
    --hairline: #dfe1e6;
    --border: rgba(38, 46, 66, 0.12);
    --accent: #4a6fa5;
    --occ: #2a78d6;
    --env: #eb6834;
    --sp: #1baf7a;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--page);
    color: var(--ink);
    font: 15px/1.6 Poppins, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
  .topnav {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 2.1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .topnav .logo img { height: 26px; width: 26px; display: block; border-radius: 6px; }
  .topnav .brand { font-weight: 700; color: #d95f00; margin-right: 0.5rem; }
  .topnav a { color: #d95f00; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .topnav .vintage { margin-left: auto; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .masthead { padding: 1.1rem 2.1rem 0.3rem; }
  h1 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.5rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  h1 em { color: #d95f00; font-style: italic; }
  .tagline {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-family: Georgia, "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", serif;
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 70rem;
  }
  .controls {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding: 0.8rem 2.1rem;
  }
  .slider-wrap { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.7rem; flex: 1; min-width: 260px; max-width: 460px; }
  .slider-wrap label { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.9rem; white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; min-width: 11.5em; }
  .slider-wrap input[type="range"] { flex: 1; accent-color: var(--accent); }
  #api-filter {
    background: var(--surface); color: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.7rem; font: inherit; font-size: 0.88rem;
    width: 16rem;
  }
  #api-filter:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; }
  .counts { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.9rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .legend { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-left: auto; }
  .swatch { width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--c); display: inline-block; }
  .line-swatch { width: 16px; height: 0; border-top: 2px solid #898781; display: inline-block; margin-left: 0.4rem; }
  .layout { display: flex; gap: 0.9rem; padding: 0 2.1rem; min-height: 480px; }
  .map-box { flex: 2.4; min-width: 0; height: 62vh; min-height: 420px; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface); }
  .panel {
    flex: 1; min-width: 280px; max-width: 400px;
    background: var(--surface); border: 1.5px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 12px; padding: 0.9rem 1rem; overflow: auto; max-height: 62vh;
  }
  .panel h2 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.02rem; }
  .panel-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8rem; margin: 0.25rem 0 0.6rem; }
  .offenders { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .offenders th { text-align: left; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); padding: 0.25rem 0.3rem; }
  .offenders td { padding: 0.34rem 0.3rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); vertical-align: top; }
  .offenders tr[data-i] { cursor: pointer; }
  .offenders tr[data-i]:hover td { background: var(--page); }
  .offenders .num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .offenders .fac { font-weight: 600; }
  .offenders .sub { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.76rem; display: block; }
  .chart-row {
    display: flex; gap: 2rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding: 1rem 2.1rem 0.4rem;
  }
  .chart-row h2 { margin: 0 0 0.3rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .chart-note { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.92rem; max-width: 26rem; margin: 0; }
  #hist { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; }
  .story {
    padding: 1.2rem 2.1rem 0.6rem;
    max-width: 72rem;
  }
  .story h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 1.1rem 0 0.4rem; }
  .story p, .story li {
    font-family: Georgia, "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", serif;
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.62;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .story ul { margin: 0.4rem 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .story li { margin: 0.4rem 0; }
  .story code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.86em;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.05em 0.3em;
  }
  .story figure { margin: 1rem 0; }
  .story figure img {
    max-width: 100%;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 10px;
  }
  .story figcaption { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  .story .muted { color: var(--ink-2); }
  footer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 1rem 2.1rem 1.4rem;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  footer p { max-width: 68rem; margin: 0.35rem auto; }
  .maplibregl-popup-content {
    font: 13px/1.45 system-ui, sans-serif;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(11, 11, 11, 0.18);
  }
  .pop-name { font-weight: 650; }
  .pop-sub { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.76rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
  .pop-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; }
  .pop-row .v { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-weight: 600; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .layout { flex-direction: column; }
    .panel { max-width: none; max-height: 40vh; }
  }

  /* family theme 2026-09-12: violet-gray page + sticky footer */
  html { height: 100%; }
  body { min-height: 100vh; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  body > footer { margin-top: auto; }

  .colophon { margin-top: 0.35rem; font-size: 0.78rem; opacity: 0.85; }
</style>
